    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5902d790_6e3df2f0",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 2208,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-02T20:06:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should be OK. I haven\u0027t worked this out in my head yet, but I\u0027m suspicious that with some refactoring, `tcpm_debug_detach` could be called less conditionally, either by moving to a different place or by checking the last state itself. This would make the module boundaries a little different than they are now, but debug detach is a workaround specific to a single TCPC, not a well defined spec concept.\n\nRight now, this is called during entry to an Unattached state and during exit from Attached.{SNK,SRC} outside of a PR Swap, if the DTS flag is set. That flag is then cleared on detach. I think if the exit calls worked, the calls entering Unattached should be redundant (see other comment about testing).\n\nSo do we need the Unattached entry calls at all? If we do, would it be sufficient to check the DTS flag? If the DTS flag is set here, how did that happen?\n\nIs the set of conditions under which we need to debug detach sufficiently regular that we could have something like `tc_debug _detach` that we call unconditionally, and that encapsulates the conditions, which we can apply at any necessary point in the state machine?",
      "revId": "ba826679c375e83c5e4453c38c02cc7e405e5a89",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7ab5ec02_3c9ba09f",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 2208,
      "author": {
        "id": 1390635
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-02T23:21:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Extracted `tc_debug_detach(port)` to encapsulate the conditions across `Unattached.{SNK,SRC}` entry and `Attached.{SNK,SRC}` exit.\n\nOn why the `Unattached` entry calls were added (https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/2786068 and https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/2792690) and why `TC_FLAGS_TS_DTS_PARTNER` isn\u0027t set there:\n1. `TC_FLAGS_TS_DTS_PARTNER` is only set when transitioning from `AttachWait.{SNK,SRC}` into `Attached.{SNK,SRC}` after `tCCDebounce`. However, the RAA489000 hardware detects DTS on the CC pins as soon as both CC lines see terminations. If a dual-role power state change forces a role switch (`Unattached.SRC \u003c-\u003e Unattached.SNK`) while an incomplete debug connection is in `AttachWait` or `Unattached`, `tc_attached_{snk,src}_exit()` never runs and `TC_FLAGS_TS_DTS_PARTNER` is not set.\n2. On initial `Unattached` entry after an EC reset or sysjump (`last_state \u003d\u003d TC_STATE_COUNT`) while the TCPC remained powered, `tc[port].flags` in EC RAM is cleared even if the TCPC hardware is still in DTS state.",
      "parentUuid": "5902d790_6e3df2f0",
      "revId": "ba826679c375e83c5e4453c38c02cc7e405e5a89",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
